1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:02,307
One, two, three, four, five, six –

2
00:00:02,332 --> 00:00:05,233
Enjoy our services and
you will get a mystery gift!

3
00:00:05,258 --> 00:00:13,691
Yes, Forty… one hundred
fifty-seven! That’s a lot of spa stars!

4
00:00:13,716 --> 00:00:17,148
That’s right! What kind of gift
do you think we’ll get for this?

5
00:00:17,173 --> 00:00:20,901
So many reward cards! You know,
my ribs here… They’re feeling better!

6
00:00:22,199 --> 00:00:24,499
- So soft, the—
- The reward cards feel amazing!

7
00:00:26,083 --> 00:00:28,609
Relaxing… oh, Kuya.

8
00:00:28,668 --> 00:00:34,381
Oh, nice, nice! So good, huh?

9
00:00:34,633 --> 00:00:37,173
That’s the employees for you!

10
00:00:37,198 --> 00:00:39,799
Like that, just like that!

11
00:00:40,129 --> 00:00:44,381
But when it’s work time, where are you?

12
00:00:44,406 --> 00:00:46,817
Massage, massage, massage!

13
00:00:48,078 --> 00:00:50,478
What kind of employees are you?!

14
00:00:50,683 --> 00:00:55,530
Kuya Aga, we’re not here for a
massage, we’re just redeeming our rewards.

15
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:56,780
- Oh, so—
- For the spa stars!

16
00:00:56,805 --> 00:01:00,197
And if you guys are… if-if-if…

17
00:01:00,556 --> 00:01:03,190
What? That’s all you ever do!

18
00:01:03,215 --> 00:01:04,780
S-s-sorry, Kuya.

19
00:01:04,805 --> 00:01:08,224
Happy New Year, boys

20
00:01:08,249 --> 00:01:11,930
! Oh, are you redeeming
your spa stars now?

21
00:01:11,955 --> 00:01:16,628
Kuya Aga, when we redeem them, we get
different prizes, there’s even a raffle.

22
00:01:16,653 --> 00:01:18,770
- Yes, correct!
- You guys and your stars!

23
00:01:18,795 --> 00:01:20,809
Alright, let’s start with yours, Chard.

24
00:01:20,834 --> 00:01:24,408
You have one, two, three,
four, five, six… twelve stars!

25
00:01:24,433 --> 00:01:27,078
Twelve stars! I worked
hard for those, Kuya Aga!

26
00:01:27,468 --> 00:01:29,762
We saved them up, Kuya Aga!

27
00:01:29,810 --> 00:01:33,136
Here, Chard! Enjoy!

28
00:01:33,161 --> 00:01:33,983
Lollipop?

29
00:01:34,515 --> 00:01:35,395
Lollipop?!

30
00:01:35,753 --> 00:01:36,866
Why a lollipop?!

31
00:01:36,981 --> 00:01:38,835
Well, you only have twelve stars.

32
00:01:38,948 --> 00:01:42,528
You should be happy, come on!
Now, for you, Iskineport. You’ve got a lot!

33
00:01:42,553 --> 00:01:43,562
Yeah, that’s a lot!

34
00:01:43,587 --> 00:01:46,325
You only get a lollipop!
You’re just one person.

35
00:01:46,350 --> 00:01:48,299
Iskineport, you got that many?

36
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:52,043
- Sorry, Kuya, but I worked hard for this.
- Me, I only got twelve stars, Kuya!

37
00:01:52,068 --> 00:01:55,421
You have four hundred
sixty-eight point seventy-five stars!

38
00:01:57,027 --> 00:01:58,961
Four hundred sixty-eight
point seventy-five stars?!

39
00:01:59,808 --> 00:02:03,876
Limited and exclusive mug from SpaKarl!

40
00:02:03,901 --> 00:02:04,796
Just a mug?!

41
00:02:04,821 --> 00:02:08,404
With all those rewards
cards, this is all I get?!

42
00:02:08,429 --> 00:02:10,940
Yeah! Isn’t it amazing?! Right?!

43
00:02:11,885 --> 00:02:15,332
Oh, oh! Kuya Aga, are you
redeeming yours now? Wait a sec!

44
00:02:15,357 --> 00:02:15,722
Huh?!

45
00:02:15,747 --> 00:02:18,552
Girls! Wait, wait!

46
00:02:18,992 --> 00:02:22,045
Kuya Aga!

47
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:23,949
- There!
- That’s a strong one!

48
00:02:23,974 --> 00:02:25,108
We present to you…

49
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:30,468
To Aga Pers, for having one thousand stars.

50
00:02:30,493 --> 00:02:32,373
SpaKarl!

51
00:02:32,649 --> 00:02:33,749
Aha!

52
00:02:34,014 --> 00:02:36,707
We got a cup, a lollipop, but you…

53
00:02:37,071 --> 00:02:39,644
A plaque?!

54
00:02:39,669 --> 00:02:45,946
No wonder you’re too tired to knead
dough, you’re always getting massages!

55
00:02:45,971 --> 00:02:47,877
Hey, stop that! Don’t be like that!

56
00:02:48,070 --> 00:02:49,796
No more body aches for you!
- Be quiet!

57
00:02:50,389 --> 00:02:51,776
- There!
- It’s your own fault…

58
00:02:51,801 --> 00:02:53,171
How did I even get this?!

59
00:02:53,196 --> 00:02:55,021
Why did you have
to give it today?!

60
00:02:55,236 --> 00:02:57,156
You could’ve done it another day!

61
00:02:57,181 --> 00:02:59,624
You’re always here?!

62
00:02:59,649 --> 00:03:01,597
I don’t come here, they just appreciate me!

63
00:04:08,174 --> 00:04:09,874
Gotcha!

64
00:04:11,406 --> 00:04:17,053
You’re not even discreet!
Kuya’s totally in love!

65
00:04:17,304 --> 00:04:18,750
Hey, what do you mean in love?!

66
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:20,122
No way!

67
00:04:20,866 --> 00:04:22,479
Oh, oh, grandson!

68
00:04:22,729 --> 00:04:24,294
Are you in love?

69
00:04:24,796 --> 00:04:26,856
Oh dear, who is it? Is it Anne?

70
00:04:27,014 --> 00:04:29,084
You’re so loud, Tash!

71
00:04:29,109 --> 00:04:30,209
It’s not—

72
00:04:30,708 --> 00:04:33,128
Then who is it? Is it Anne?

73
00:04:33,859 --> 00:04:35,112
Yes, Lola Maxi.

74
00:04:36,632 --> 00:04:38,752
But keep it a secret, okay?
Don’t tell anyone, please.

75
00:04:38,777 --> 00:04:41,230
Why does it have to be a secret?

76
00:04:41,536 --> 00:04:46,053
What’s wrong with it?
Anne is such a lovely girl!

77
00:04:46,279 --> 00:04:48,673
And I totally approve of her!

78
00:04:48,698 --> 00:04:53,766
You know, when it comes to love,
you should shout it to the world!

79
00:04:53,790 --> 00:05:00,416
Look at your Grandpa Roman, he wanted the
whole world to know how much he loved me!

80
00:05:00,589 --> 00:05:02,476
That’s how it should be!

81
00:05:02,501 --> 00:05:03,795
Oh, Lola’s right!

82
00:05:04,450 --> 00:05:06,470
Actually, why are you keeping it a secret?

83
00:05:06,549 --> 00:05:07,269
Yeah?

84
00:05:07,756 --> 00:05:08,389
Ah!

85
00:05:09,058 --> 00:05:10,024
Aha!

86
00:05:10,463 --> 00:05:13,270
You don’t want Mom and Dad to know, do you?

87
00:05:13,374 --> 00:05:14,154
It’s not that.

88
00:05:14,991 --> 00:05:18,451
It’s just… Anne and I haven’t
really talked about it clearly.

89
00:05:18,805 --> 00:05:21,999
Yeah, we have mutual understanding, but
I’m not sure if we’re really together yet,

90
00:05:22,597 --> 00:05:26,151
and I don’t want to assume
something that isn’t real.

91
00:05:26,612 --> 00:05:29,439
That’s exactly why you should talk!

92
00:05:29,487 --> 00:05:32,199
So things are clear, right?

93
00:05:32,243 --> 00:05:34,543
Not this whole secret-secret thing!

94
00:05:34,568 --> 00:05:36,043
That’s risky, oh dear!

95
00:05:36,068 --> 00:05:37,480
What? What did I just hear?

96
00:05:37,505 --> 00:05:40,297
Secret-secret? What secret-secret?

97
00:05:40,517 --> 00:05:42,244
What, Andres? Andres? What?

98
00:05:42,269 --> 00:05:45,389
Oh no, oh no! Alright,
you don’t want to say it?

99
00:05:45,806 --> 00:05:47,219
I’ll just tell them myself.

100
00:05:47,244 --> 00:05:48,475
- Go ahead, Lola Maxi.
- Lola Maxi—

101
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:49,601
You know, Cha…

102
00:05:54,164 --> 00:05:55,991
What was it again? I think I forgot?

103
00:05:56,016 --> 00:05:58,090
Oh yeah, you’re right, Lola!

104
00:05:58,146 --> 00:06:03,886
Weren’t you supposed to teach us
your secret cheesy ensaymada recipe?

105
00:06:04,161 --> 00:06:05,168
Now’s the time!

106
00:06:05,193 --> 00:06:06,885
Oh, yes, Lola! That’s right!

107
00:06:06,910 --> 00:06:08,769
- So exciting!
- That’s right, Lola! Let’s go, let’s go!

108
00:06:11,322 --> 00:06:12,948
- We’re official?
- We’re really official?

109
00:06:13,454 --> 00:06:16,800
You know, we could
always sleep on it first, right?

110
00:06:16,873 --> 00:06:17,607
That’s true, true.

111
00:06:18,032 --> 00:06:19,859
That way, we can think about it more.

112
00:06:19,949 --> 00:06:23,862
At least we know we have
mutual understanding, right?

113
00:06:24,095 --> 00:06:25,197
Mm-mm!

114
00:06:25,222 --> 00:06:26,895
Mutual understanding.

115
00:06:27,322 --> 00:06:28,298
MU.

116
00:06:33,459 --> 00:06:34,699
Look at her!

117
00:06:35,614 --> 00:06:38,101
Looks like Andres is living rent-free
in someone’s mind again, huh?

118
00:06:38,782 --> 00:06:41,168
Huh? What do you mean living rent-free?

119
00:06:41,196 --> 00:06:43,656
See? He’s been smiling nonstop!

120
00:06:43,681 --> 00:06:44,969
Excuse me, can I ask something?

121
00:06:45,769 --> 00:06:47,955
Where’s Beauty’s shop?

122
00:06:48,530 --> 00:06:49,930
Oh, Boss Beauty?

123
00:06:50,592 --> 00:06:52,152
Over there… by the court.

124
00:06:52,754 --> 00:06:53,420
Just keep going straight.

125
00:06:53,957 --> 00:06:56,884
Oh, okay. Thanks! I’m Ash, by the way.

126
00:06:56,909 --> 00:06:57,686
Hi.

127
00:06:57,711 --> 00:06:58,596
Hi.

128
00:06:59,442 --> 00:07:01,100
Wait, let’s go back to that.

129
00:07:02,622 --> 00:07:03,775
Are you guys together now?

130
00:07:06,438 --> 00:07:07,830
Have you held hands?

131
00:07:07,855 --> 00:07:10,409
Huh? No.

132
00:07:11,188 --> 00:07:12,120
Really?

133
00:07:12,145 --> 00:07:14,142
But for sure, you’ve gone on a date?

134
00:07:15,485 --> 00:07:16,447
No.

135
00:07:17,235 --> 00:07:19,029
For sure… you’ve kissed, right?

136
00:07:19,079 --> 00:07:20,892
What?! No way!

137
00:07:20,954 --> 00:07:22,241
Then what are you?!

138
00:07:22,266 --> 00:07:23,387
Assuming!

139
00:07:23,493 --> 00:07:26,174
That’s what you are!
Assuming! That’s risky!

140
00:07:26,525 --> 00:07:28,373
What if you’re the only one
who thinks there’s something,

141
00:07:28,397 --> 00:07:30,045
but actually, there’s
nothing, nothing, nothing!

142
00:07:31,539 --> 00:07:33,139
Relax, take it easy.

143
00:07:33,898 --> 00:07:36,698
Alright, I’ll head out now. Thanks again!

144
00:07:36,723 --> 00:07:37,636
Bye!

145
00:07:39,354 --> 00:07:42,220
- They’ve been through a lot.
- I know, I can tell.

146
00:07:44,772 --> 00:07:46,345
Hey, are you okay?

147
00:07:47,225 --> 00:07:48,244
Hey!

148
00:07:49,804 --> 00:07:50,817
Is it true, cousin?

149
00:07:51,595 --> 00:07:53,580
Do you have a lot of
patients who pass away?

150
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:56,827
It’s inevitable.

151
00:07:56,878 --> 00:08:00,015
So, you know when someone’s going
to die, or when they’re close to dying?

152
00:08:00,410 --> 00:08:02,010
- Yeah.
- Really?

153
00:08:02,035 --> 00:08:03,853
So, what about this one?
When do you think they’ll die?

154
00:08:04,759 --> 00:08:07,005
Boss Beauty, come on! Why me again?!

155
00:08:07,030 --> 00:08:08,712
Well, you look like you’re about to go!

156
00:08:08,978 --> 00:08:12,144
You should be grateful I can see you—other
people, you just haunt them, right?

157
00:08:12,169 --> 00:08:16,027
- Hey, hey! Happy New Year!
- Happy New Year!

158
00:08:16,314 --> 00:08:17,395
Boss Beauty!

159
00:08:17,420 --> 00:08:19,053
Oh, Kuya Aga? Happy New Year!

160
00:08:19,078 --> 00:08:20,913
Happy New Year! I was
hoping to borrow some…

161
00:08:20,937 --> 00:08:22,771
actually, I was going
to ask for a loan…

162
00:08:23,215 --> 00:08:26,371
Kuya Aga, you know I love
you, but come on… first day

163
00:08:26,534 --> 00:08:29,691
of the year, and you’re
already asking for a loan?

164
00:08:29,716 --> 00:08:33,759
Ah, I get it, it’s January
again. Everyone’s broke.

165
00:08:33,784 --> 00:08:35,470
Happy New Year, bro!

166
00:08:35,512 --> 00:08:37,632
- Hey!
- BFF, happy new year!

167
00:08:37,657 --> 00:08:38,372
- BFF!
- Tso K!

168
00:08:38,397 --> 00:08:40,345
- Yes!
- Happy new year!

169
00:08:40,995 --> 00:08:41,862
Happy new year!

170
00:08:41,887 --> 00:08:43,775
- You’re in such a good mood!
- Yeah, I am!

171
00:08:44,256 --> 00:08:47,979
Nothing! You know,
BFF, I realized that this year,

172
00:08:48,003 --> 00:08:51,726
I should let go of all the bad vibes.

173
00:08:51,881 --> 00:08:55,244
No more fights, no more negativity.

174
00:08:55,269 --> 00:09:00,050
And my wish for you this year… I
wish you the best and happiness.

175
00:09:00,075 --> 00:09:02,683
Ah, Boss Beauty…

176
00:09:03,122 --> 00:09:03,769
Mmm, Kuya?

177
00:09:03,794 --> 00:09:06,875
If you can’t lend me money, it’s okay.

178
00:09:07,594 --> 00:09:11,087
Wait, wait, wait. Hold up. BFF, a loan?

179
00:09:11,249 --> 00:09:12,290
You’re borrowing money?

180
00:09:12,315 --> 00:09:15,141
No… it’s just… for bakery expenses.

181
00:09:15,232 --> 00:09:17,145
Nope, nope… you’re not borrowing money.

182
00:09:17,731 --> 00:09:18,781
- Boss Beauty!
- Yes?

183
00:09:18,806 --> 00:09:23,690
Give Aga everything
he needs. I’ll pay for it!

184
00:09:23,743 --> 00:09:26,716
- Ah, move, move, move!
- Chef K!

185
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:30,156
Hug, hug! Thank you
so much! Thank you!

186
00:09:31,243 --> 00:09:32,530
- BFF!
- Yes?

187
00:09:32,803 --> 00:09:35,390
You’ve been hugging
me a lot recently, I noticed.

188
00:09:35,415 --> 00:09:37,508
Oh you’re too much, I’m
just really thankful for you.

189
00:09:37,533 --> 00:09:38,776
Ah, okay, okay!

190
00:09:39,423 --> 00:09:40,484
Wait… really?

191
00:09:41,608 --> 00:09:44,535
I’ll really pay for it! That’s
how much I love you!

192
00:09:44,754 --> 00:09:46,414
I’m so happy, I’m so happy!

193
00:09:48,731 --> 00:09:52,231
No, I’m just really excited!
Oh, by the way, who’s this?

194
00:09:52,256 --> 00:09:54,176
Oh, my cousin!

195
00:09:54,676 --> 00:09:55,663
My cousin, Kuya Aga.

196
00:09:55,718 --> 00:09:58,204
He’s a caregiver abroad.

197
00:09:58,229 --> 00:09:59,556
He just came back to
the Philippines because

198
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:00,908
the person he was taking
care of passed away.

199
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:03,702
- Ah, hello, hello, hello!
- Hello!

200
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:06,689
Hey! Wait a minute,
anyway, hello… ah, things

201
00:10:06,713 --> 00:10:09,562
just get a little chaotic
sometimes… hoo!

202
00:10:10,289 --> 00:10:11,822
Okay, what was that?!

203
00:10:12,193 --> 00:10:13,533
- Nothing, I just went for it.
- Is this free?!

204
00:10:13,558 --> 00:10:15,023
- It’s on me.
- Oh, thanks!

205
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:17,767
- That’s how much I love you, friend!
- Thank you, thank you so much!

206
00:10:17,792 --> 00:10:18,854
- Yeah.
- Thanks!

207
00:10:18,879 --> 00:10:21,166
- Hey! Let’s grab the groceries!
- Let’s go get them!

208
00:10:21,197 --> 00:10:22,827
Why do you keep coming back?

209
00:10:22,852 --> 00:10:23,694
So generous!

210
00:10:23,719 --> 00:10:27,573
I was talking about
Aga, okay? Not you guys!

211
00:10:27,604 --> 00:10:28,752
Take everything you need!

212
00:10:28,777 --> 00:10:29,677
Wow!

213
00:10:29,702 --> 00:10:32,454
Kuya, we already got so
much! Thank you, Tso K!

214
00:10:32,479 --> 00:10:33,507
Wait a minute!

215
00:10:34,902 --> 00:10:35,675
Oh, what’s that?!

216
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:38,392
Hey, hey, why… hey! That
was loud! That was loud!

217
00:10:43,137 --> 00:10:45,804
Hi, Orb… Have you eaten?

218
00:10:56,397 --> 00:10:57,468
Hi, Orb!

219
00:10:59,141 --> 00:11:00,328
Where are you?

220
00:11:09,492 --> 00:11:10,538
Ugh!

221
00:11:11,147 --> 00:11:13,173
What if I really am assuming things?

222
00:11:16,339 --> 00:11:17,405
This is so hard!

223
00:11:25,312 --> 00:11:26,362
Tada!

224
00:11:27,015 --> 00:11:28,082
We’re here!

225
00:11:28,348 --> 00:11:29,828
What should I say, Tash?

226
00:11:30,399 --> 00:11:31,318
Maybe this—

227
00:11:31,343 --> 00:11:34,203
Um, Orb, can we talk?

228
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:36,100
Wait, wait, no.

229
00:11:36,375 --> 00:11:37,775
I mean Anne, right?

230
00:11:39,163 --> 00:11:41,349
Ugh, help me out here, Tash, come on!

231
00:11:41,374 --> 00:11:43,910
Relax!

232
00:11:44,259 --> 00:11:46,479
You’re best friends, right?

233
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:49,553
That means you and Anne
already have a foundation.

234
00:11:49,868 --> 00:11:55,602
In other words, all you have to do
is talk to her like you normally would!

235
00:12:00,701 --> 00:12:01,221
How, though?

236
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:04,083
I’m scared. I should just go
home, Tash! I can’t do this.

237
00:12:04,108 --> 00:12:06,824
Um, no, no, no, no, no.
You’re not going home.

238
00:12:06,849 --> 00:12:11,622
We’re already here, so
don’t waste this chance, okay?

239
00:12:12,153 --> 00:12:13,080
Yeah, yeah.

240
00:12:14,713 --> 00:12:15,119
Orb!

241
00:12:15,144 --> 00:12:15,643
Orb!

242
00:12:19,018 --> 00:12:19,438
Hi!

243
00:12:21,019 --> 00:12:21,659
Hi!

244
00:12:25,973 --> 00:12:26,633
Hi!

245
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:28,965
Hi? That’s it? Just hi?

246
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:33,482
I can’t do this, guys, I’m
going home. Bye, sorry!

247
00:12:35,288 --> 00:12:36,442
Hey, wait!

248
00:12:42,769 --> 00:12:44,189
BFF, this is all for you guys.

249
00:12:44,542 --> 00:12:45,529
Huh?

250
00:12:45,834 --> 00:12:46,301
Lola.

251
00:12:46,326 --> 00:12:47,898
- Are you serious, Karl?!
- Yes, yes.

252
00:12:48,582 --> 00:12:51,369
- Wow!
- This feels different.

253
00:12:51,394 --> 00:12:52,373
Wow!

254
00:12:55,038 --> 00:12:56,351
Is that really Tso K?

255
00:12:57,578 --> 00:13:02,712
I can’t believe it! He’s acting so
nice, but he used to be the worst!

256
00:13:04,591 --> 00:13:05,938
And why is he like that?

257
00:13:05,963 --> 00:13:12,335
I bet he’s just pretending to be nice
because he’s up to something with Kuya Aga.

258
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:14,110
Oh no, what do we do?!

259
00:13:14,135 --> 00:13:15,939
Oh, come on! You’re overreacting!

260
00:13:15,964 --> 00:13:19,400
You’re too much! But
seriously, guys, calm down!

261
00:13:19,425 --> 00:13:22,639
Can’t my Tso K just be nice for real?

262
00:13:22,664 --> 00:13:24,431
And guess what?

263
00:13:24,456 --> 00:13:27,215
He even gave out bonuses at SpaKarl!

264
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:28,495
- Oh?!
- Right?!

265
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:30,090
- Bonuses?
- Nice!

266
00:13:30,115 --> 00:13:33,352
See? That’s not the
real Tso K! He’s all about

267
00:13:33,377 --> 00:13:37,945
money, and now he’s
giving out bonuses?

268
00:13:38,965 --> 00:13:41,733
Oh no, guys, this only means one thing.

269
00:13:41,990 --> 00:13:44,084
- He’s about to die!
- Huh?!

270
00:13:45,048 --> 00:13:47,294
Yeah! All my patients were like that.

271
00:13:47,455 --> 00:13:53,187
Super mean, but once they know
their time is up, they suddenly turn nice!

272
00:13:53,314 --> 00:13:54,061
BFF…

273
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:56,420
What? What do you want?

274
00:13:57,213 --> 00:13:59,219
This is too much, thank you!

275
00:13:59,244 --> 00:13:59,977
- Yeah!
- No…

276
00:14:00,002 --> 00:14:01,042
- Karl!
- Thank you!

277
00:14:01,113 --> 00:14:01,858
It’s okay.

278
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:05,279
This is too much, I feel bad!

279
00:14:05,383 --> 00:14:08,050
No, really, it’s fine.

280
00:14:08,081 --> 00:14:11,406
I just want to make sure you
all have everything you need.

281
00:14:11,431 --> 00:14:14,586
Why are you guys thinking
like this? You’re like family to me!

282
00:14:14,611 --> 00:14:16,365
It’s just that…

283
00:14:16,569 --> 00:14:22,028
Karl, seriously, thank you!
May the Lord bless you.

284
00:14:22,053 --> 00:14:23,768
Thank you, Lola Maxi.

285
00:14:23,793 --> 00:14:29,339
You know, I realized it’s always
better to do good because life is short.

286
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:35,560
And as they say, we can’t
take all this with us to heaven.

287
00:14:37,531 --> 00:14:41,744
See?! I told you! He’s on his way out!

288
00:14:44,237 --> 00:14:45,910
Poor Tso K!

289
00:14:48,493 --> 00:14:52,160
So after everything, he’s
just gonna ignore me?!

290
00:14:52,693 --> 00:14:53,526
Hey, Anne!

291
00:14:53,551 --> 00:14:55,098
Anne! Wait!

292
00:14:55,711 --> 00:14:56,918
Leave me alone!

293
00:14:58,180 --> 00:14:59,353
Come on, friend!

294
00:15:00,809 --> 00:15:02,196
Don’t worry, Anne.

295
00:15:02,221 --> 00:15:07,957
If you and Andres aren’t meant
to be, I’ll take care of him for you!

296
00:15:08,345 --> 00:15:09,052
You too?!

297
00:15:09,077 --> 00:15:11,451
Look at that, Francis is after me!

298
00:15:11,988 --> 00:15:13,228
Ugh! Another one!

299
00:15:14,138 --> 00:15:18,810
You know, Anne, maybe Andres
just panicked, that’s why he left. Right?

300
00:15:18,877 --> 00:15:19,855
Mm-mm!

301
00:15:23,585 --> 00:15:26,311
You know what? Ash is right.

302
00:15:27,707 --> 00:15:29,861
Maybe I really am assuming too much.

303
00:15:30,877 --> 00:15:33,317
Because Andres? He’s such a player!

304
00:15:33,924 --> 00:15:36,237
All guys are players!

305
00:15:36,871 --> 00:15:41,337
See?! I told you! But no
one ever listens to me!

306
00:15:42,598 --> 00:15:47,138
Oh, guys, so you’ve already
met Boss Beauty’s cousin!

307
00:15:47,163 --> 00:15:48,425
Cousin?!

308
00:15:49,266 --> 00:15:50,293
Why?

309
00:15:50,632 --> 00:15:51,765
Don’t you believe it?

310
00:15:51,838 --> 00:15:53,058
No!

311
00:15:53,689 --> 00:15:57,049
Kuya, can you stop already?

312
00:15:57,699 --> 00:15:59,599
You’re making me dizzy!

313
00:15:59,624 --> 00:16:00,881
Tash, what do I need to do?

314
00:16:02,367 --> 00:16:03,387
Oh, is that so?

315
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:05,239
That looks good!

316
00:16:05,406 --> 00:16:06,572
Go up to Anne.

317
00:16:06,806 --> 00:16:07,342
Okay…?

318
00:16:07,367 --> 00:16:09,920
Then, ask her…

319
00:16:10,298 --> 00:16:11,184
Hmmm?

320
00:16:11,904 --> 00:16:13,293
Will you be my girlfriend?

321
00:16:13,541 --> 00:16:14,908
Oh, like that?

322
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:17,028
That doesn’t
sound like it’ll work.

323
00:16:17,691 --> 00:16:19,102
- Andres!
- Mmm?

324
00:16:20,115 --> 00:16:21,895
What’s your problem? A girl, huh?

325
00:16:25,810 --> 00:16:27,817
Yes, Kuya Iskineport, it’s about a girl.

326
00:16:27,842 --> 00:16:30,016
Ugh, and you’re asking Tasha?

327
00:16:30,331 --> 00:16:32,424
You should be asking me about women!

328
00:16:32,449 --> 00:16:36,099
Haven’t you heard? I’m an
expert when it comes to chicks.

329
00:16:36,285 --> 00:16:39,522
- Oh, really? That’s a lot to claim!
- Of course! Good thing I’ve changed!

330
00:16:39,547 --> 00:16:41,253
- So what should I do?
- It’s Anne, right?

331
00:16:41,908 --> 00:16:42,836
Yeah?

332
00:16:42,861 --> 00:16:45,327
Okay, stand up. Pretend you’re Anne.

333
00:16:47,837 --> 00:16:51,563
I’ll be me. You see Anne, right?

334
00:16:52,152 --> 00:16:53,188
Go up to her.

335
00:16:58,119 --> 00:17:00,366
There, act all cute. Do this.

336
00:17:00,942 --> 00:17:02,056
Then, look into her eyes.

337
00:17:02,135 --> 00:17:03,749
Wow, that’s intense!

338
00:17:04,635 --> 00:17:05,862
Of course, it’s intense.

339
00:17:06,425 --> 00:17:09,925
I need to be gorgeous while
doing it. Stop interrupting!

340
00:17:09,950 --> 00:17:11,225
I’m getting into this!

341
00:17:11,306 --> 00:17:12,866
Look here.

342
00:17:13,327 --> 00:17:16,991
When you do that, right there…

343
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,253
you lean in.

344
00:17:20,428 --> 00:17:21,328
Kiss her.

345
00:17:22,798 --> 00:17:24,885
Hold her. There! She’ll hold on to you!

346
00:17:25,026 --> 00:17:27,180
She’ll cling to you on her own!

347
00:17:36,779 --> 00:17:38,519
Oh, Mariposa?

348
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:40,574
How’s SpaKarl?

349
00:17:44,707 --> 00:17:46,987
It’s okay, Tso K!

350
00:17:47,813 --> 00:17:52,609
You don’t have to worry
anymore, I promise I’ll

351
00:17:52,653 --> 00:17:57,449
take care of SpaKarl
no matter what happens!

352
00:17:58,812 --> 00:17:59,738
O-o-okay?

353
00:17:59,763 --> 00:18:02,307
Sorry! Sorry! I can’t do this!

354
00:18:04,588 --> 00:18:05,713
Wh–what was that?

355
00:18:05,885 --> 00:18:07,260
Why are you crying?

356
00:18:07,508 --> 00:18:17,119
Tso K, here’s your store
list from my supply shop.

357
00:18:17,862 --> 00:18:19,849
I took off all my markups.

358
00:18:20,466 --> 00:18:21,327
Whoa!

359
00:18:21,352 --> 00:18:22,774
You’re only paying the retail price!

360
00:18:22,799 --> 00:18:23,805
- Really?
- Yeah!

361
00:18:23,830 --> 00:18:25,549
Wow, thanks, thanks!

362
00:18:26,149 --> 00:18:26,842
Okay!

363
00:18:26,867 --> 00:18:30,000
Thank you! But why are you crying?

364
00:18:30,025 --> 00:18:31,792
And why does it look like
everyone else is crying too?

365
00:18:31,857 --> 00:18:35,810
Tso K, thank you! Thank you so much!

366
00:18:36,212 --> 00:18:39,018
Hey! What is this? Wait,
what’s going on here?

367
00:18:39,149 --> 00:18:41,896
I can’t do this! I can’t take it, Tso K!

368
00:18:42,642 --> 00:18:44,075
What did you all take?

369
00:18:44,398 --> 00:18:45,785
Did you eat MSG or something?

370
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:48,713
Why are you all acting crazy and crying?

371
00:18:48,738 --> 00:18:49,991
What happened?!

372
00:18:51,435 --> 00:18:52,642
It’s okay, Tso K.

373
00:18:53,623 --> 00:18:55,816
Don’t worry about it, just rest.

374
00:18:57,801 --> 00:19:01,900
Yeah, yeah, you’re always worrying.

375
00:19:05,171 --> 00:19:06,361
Oh, you girls?

376
00:19:07,279 --> 00:19:08,346
You good?

377
00:19:11,277 --> 00:19:13,964
Hey! What?

378
00:19:14,299 --> 00:19:15,979
Thank you, Tso K!

379
00:19:16,004 --> 00:19:17,632
Why thank you?

380
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:19,804
What happened to you
guys? Why are you crying?

381
00:19:21,108 --> 00:19:26,539
I told you not to take weird
stuff! Alright, alright, go on!

382
00:19:26,564 --> 00:19:28,806
- Tso K…
- Just go.

383
00:19:28,837 --> 00:19:30,723
- Do you want it to be us instead?
- Us instead?

384
00:19:32,632 --> 00:19:33,931
Hold up! See?

385
00:19:33,968 --> 00:19:36,574
You keep taking things and
now you’re running after me!

386
00:19:36,599 --> 00:19:38,488
You already know you
all look like monsters!

387
00:19:38,513 --> 00:19:40,696
Get out of here, stop bothering me!

388
00:19:40,856 --> 00:19:42,202
Here, take this instead.

389
00:19:42,884 --> 00:19:45,290
What’s happening? Why is everyone crying?

390
00:19:45,315 --> 00:19:47,511
Tso K, don’t mind them.

391
00:19:47,536 --> 00:19:51,682
You know, I’m really grateful I got
to know you, even for a short time.

392
00:19:52,263 --> 00:19:54,343
Just enjoy your life, okay?

393
00:19:54,523 --> 00:19:55,628
Get some rest.

394
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:57,120
You too, get some rest!

395
00:19:57,542 --> 00:20:00,562
Wh–why would I rest?
I still have a business to run!

396
00:20:00,587 --> 00:20:01,715
What are you all talking about?

397
00:20:12,798 --> 00:20:13,806
See?

398
00:20:14,859 --> 00:20:20,595
So it’s true that my BFF is terminally ill?

399
00:20:20,744 --> 00:20:23,417
Oh no, poor Karl!

400
00:20:23,442 --> 00:20:24,157
It’s true?!

401
00:20:24,227 --> 00:20:29,704
Yes. Ate Cha, you know, Ate Cha,
Tso K suddenly changed completely.

402
00:20:30,404 --> 00:20:35,718
Oh, maybe he really needs prayers, who
knows? Maybe a miracle could still happen.

403
00:20:37,123 --> 00:20:41,743
Wait, did you actually see the results
saying he’s sick? That he’s dying?

404
00:20:41,883 --> 00:20:42,936
No, Kuya.

405
00:20:43,304 --> 00:20:45,817
But Ash said those are
the signs when someone is

406
00:20:45,841 --> 00:20:50,216
about to be taken by the
Lord… they start acting nice.

407
00:20:50,347 --> 00:20:51,938
- Taken?
- When they’re about to be taken!

408
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:59,606
So there’s no actual result yet, and
you’re all already assuming he’s dying?

409
00:20:59,631 --> 00:21:01,106
This is all just gossip!

410
00:21:02,525 --> 00:21:06,058
Never mind…hold on, I need to talk to BFF.

411
00:21:06,165 --> 00:21:07,493
Okay, my love?

412
00:21:07,741 --> 00:21:10,858
Lola Maxi. I need to talk to BFF.

413
00:21:11,450 --> 00:21:12,767
- BFF!
- Here we go!

414
00:21:12,842 --> 00:21:14,675
- BFF! BFF!
- Sorry, did I scare you?

415
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:17,563
Oh, no, not at all! BFF, sit, sit, sit.

416
00:21:17,729 --> 00:21:19,729
Hold on! I just want to ask you something…

417
00:21:19,754 --> 00:21:20,626
Huh?

418
00:21:20,895 --> 00:21:23,069
Maybe you and Cha want to go out?

419
00:21:23,426 --> 00:21:25,612
I’ll treat you to a movie!

420
00:21:25,637 --> 00:21:26,767
Whoa! A movie?

421
00:21:27,252 --> 00:21:30,357
Cha, what do you think? A movie! My treat!

422
00:21:30,382 --> 00:21:32,562
- I just watched Uninvited, though!
- Really?!

423
00:21:33,430 --> 00:21:34,576
So, you don’t want to?

424
00:21:35,050 --> 00:21:39,717
No, uh… BFF, I actually
wanted to talk to you.

425
00:21:39,742 --> 00:21:40,817
Why? Is there a problem?

426
00:21:40,915 --> 00:21:44,042
No, not really! There’s just
something I want to ask you.

427
00:21:56,363 --> 00:21:57,330
Is there a problem?

428
00:21:57,355 --> 00:22:00,809
- No, BFF, no.
- You look like you’re deep in thought.

429
00:22:02,590 --> 00:22:04,343
I just wanted to ask you something.

430
00:22:04,368 --> 00:22:06,005
Oh? What is it?

431
00:22:07,237 --> 00:22:08,468
Don’t be shocked, okay?

432
00:22:13,328 --> 00:22:17,168
BFF… have you eaten?

433
00:22:19,914 --> 00:22:21,360
For real? No, not yet.

434
00:22:21,385 --> 00:22:23,915
- Oh, maybe—wait, hold on!
- That’s it?!

435
00:22:23,953 --> 00:22:28,460
- Of course, of course, of course!
- Not yet, I haven’t eaten!

436
00:22:28,485 --> 00:22:30,091
Alright, alright, we’ll get food!

437
00:22:30,122 --> 00:22:31,969
I thought you were gonna
ask something serious…

438
00:22:31,994 --> 00:22:32,743
Nothing, really!

439
00:22:32,768 --> 00:22:33,981
- We got this.
- Alright.

440
00:22:35,768 --> 00:22:36,388
Cha!

441
00:22:36,419 --> 00:22:38,446
Here, here. Juice for you too!

442
00:22:38,472 --> 00:22:40,099
Wow, straight to juice, huh?

443
00:22:46,650 --> 00:22:48,057
- BFF!
- Oh, BFF?

444
00:22:48,774 --> 00:22:50,152
- How are you?
- Okay.

445
00:22:52,512 --> 00:22:53,421
Are you okay?

446
00:22:53,446 --> 00:22:54,540
You, are you okay?

447
00:22:54,892 --> 00:22:56,085
- Huh?
- Why do you look like that?

448
00:22:56,885 --> 00:22:58,024
Is there a problem?

449
00:22:58,663 --> 00:23:00,116
Ah, I know!

450
00:23:01,099 --> 00:23:03,459
You probably sold out
all your goods, right?

451
00:23:03,894 --> 00:23:07,980
Come on, let’s buy some.

452
00:23:08,410 --> 00:23:10,804
Ah, no, no, it’s not that, not that.

453
00:23:10,829 --> 00:23:13,168
Ah, no, I don’t have a
problem with that. Ah…

454
00:23:19,625 --> 00:23:20,672
ah…

455
00:23:26,577 --> 00:23:27,790
- BFF…
- Oh?

456
00:23:29,589 --> 00:23:31,529
I just want to say sorry.

457
00:23:32,320 --> 00:23:33,413
For your understanding.

458
00:23:33,943 --> 00:23:37,056
You know, for our past misunderstandings.

459
00:23:38,109 --> 00:23:39,522
Especially about Cha.

460
00:23:40,726 --> 00:23:41,826
Just know that we love you.

461
00:23:42,621 --> 00:23:43,682
We love you.

462
00:23:45,222 --> 00:23:47,589
That’s why I’m making it up
to you. Me too, I feel the same.

463
00:23:48,581 --> 00:23:51,301
I don’t like holding grudges.

464
00:23:52,949 --> 00:23:54,422
BFF, life is short.

465
00:23:55,035 --> 00:23:57,168
I don’t want to fill myself with anger.

466
00:23:57,796 --> 00:23:58,423
Exactly!

467
00:23:58,448 --> 00:24:00,229
That’s what I’m saying. Life is short.

468
00:24:00,254 --> 00:24:02,814
That’s why I want you
to know that no matter

469
00:24:02,838 --> 00:24:05,472
what happens, as long
as we’re alive, okay?

470
00:24:05,636 --> 00:24:08,975
Me, my spouse, my
family—as long as we’re in this world,

471
00:24:08,999 --> 00:24:12,407
you can count
on us to be here for you.

472
00:24:12,768 --> 00:24:15,188
Especially Anne.

473
00:24:17,115 --> 00:24:20,028
We’ll treat Anne like our own child.

474
00:24:20,481 --> 00:24:21,460
That’s it!

475
00:24:22,055 --> 00:24:24,195
That’s what I want to hear, BFF.

476
00:24:27,769 --> 00:24:29,936
BFF, give me a hug.

477
00:24:30,514 --> 00:24:32,433
Of course, of course.

478
00:24:34,281 --> 00:24:36,680
Thank you! Love you, BFF!

479
00:24:36,705 --> 00:24:37,845
Love you, BFF!

480
00:24:37,870 --> 00:24:38,898
Love you. Thank you, okay?

481
00:24:39,395 --> 00:24:40,343
Thank you.

482
00:24:42,262 --> 00:24:46,208
It’s different, BFF, when
friends truly support each other.

483
00:24:46,233 --> 00:24:48,050
- Yes!
- I can feel that.

484
00:24:48,075 --> 00:24:49,030
Yes, yes.

485
00:24:49,090 --> 00:24:50,423
I know that’s how it is.

486
00:24:50,448 --> 00:24:51,234
Yes, BFF.

487
00:24:51,259 --> 00:24:53,824
You’re the only friend
who’s been like this to me.

488
00:24:53,849 --> 00:24:54,348
Don’t go far.

489
00:24:54,373 --> 00:24:56,241
- Okay.
- I haven’t fully taken it in yet.

490
00:24:56,266 --> 00:24:57,308
BFF…

491
00:24:57,651 --> 00:24:58,652
BFF.

492
00:24:59,330 --> 00:25:01,470
I’m still letting it sink in. Huh?

493
00:25:02,188 --> 00:25:05,075
Ouch, ouch! What the heck!

494
00:25:09,850 --> 00:25:10,703
What was that?

495
00:25:10,848 --> 00:25:13,328
Just messing around. Just messing
around. Just messing around.

496
00:25:17,277 --> 00:25:19,183
Tso K, knock-knock!

497
00:25:19,423 --> 00:25:20,404
Who’s there?

498
00:25:22,049 --> 00:25:23,083
Has the train arrived yet?

499
00:25:23,364 --> 00:25:25,571
Oh, there it is! Toooot!

500
00:25:25,596 --> 00:25:29,216
Tso K, Tso K, Tso
K, Tso K, Tso K!

501
00:25:35,270 --> 00:25:38,842
Tso K, what does the "K"
in your name stand for?

502
00:25:39,149 --> 00:25:40,002
What?!

503
00:25:40,027 --> 00:25:41,122
Death!

504
00:25:43,681 --> 00:25:44,428
Ah!

505
00:25:44,453 --> 00:25:46,898
Just kidding! It stands for laughter!

506
00:25:49,803 --> 00:25:50,777
Ouch!

507
00:25:58,496 --> 00:26:00,836
Orb, can we please talk?

508
00:26:01,515 --> 00:26:03,322
There’s nothing to talk about.

509
00:26:04,521 --> 00:26:08,549
You completely ignored me yesterday!
You acted like I didn’t exist!

510
00:26:11,888 --> 00:26:13,661
Girl, I’m telling you,
he’s just leading you on!

511
00:26:14,927 --> 00:26:18,626
Guys, come on. Stop.

512
00:26:19,645 --> 00:26:22,818
Oh, so you really called for backup, huh?

513
00:26:23,213 --> 00:26:25,130
Hey, okay, wait, Anne.

514
00:26:25,155 --> 00:26:28,828
Let Andres explain. Trust me, okay?

515
00:26:29,294 --> 00:26:30,134
Explain?!

516
00:26:30,436 --> 00:26:31,499
Explain what –

517
00:26:32,171 --> 00:26:33,640
why you’ve been avoiding me?

518
00:26:34,819 --> 00:26:35,788
Why?

519
00:26:37,718 --> 00:26:38,958
Do I have bad breath?

520
00:26:40,666 --> 00:26:41,713
Do I smell bad?!

521
00:26:45,045 --> 00:26:46,179
So why?!

522
00:26:46,224 --> 00:26:47,571
Why are you avoiding me?!

523
00:26:48,133 --> 00:26:49,706
Because I don’t know what we are!

524
00:26:50,451 --> 00:26:56,677
Orb, I respect you and care for
you, and I just don’t know my place.

525
00:26:58,335 --> 00:27:02,337
And I got scared that I might make
you think I’m taking advantage of you.

526
00:27:03,282 --> 00:27:04,404
That’s why.

527
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:07,736
You don’t know what we are?

528
00:27:08,564 --> 00:27:09,748
We’re together!

529
00:27:10,260 --> 00:27:12,306
And you’re over there saying
“I don’t know, I don’t know”?!

530
00:27:12,506 --> 00:27:13,482
Really?!

531
00:27:13,927 --> 00:27:14,826
We’re together!

532
00:27:15,231 --> 00:27:17,018
Oh yeah!

533
00:27:17,043 --> 00:27:19,239
Hey, everyone, Orb and I are official!

534
00:27:22,102 --> 00:27:25,209
Sssh! Tso K might hear you!

535
00:27:25,626 --> 00:27:29,596
Oh, right. Sorry, sorry, sorry. Yeah, okay.

536
00:27:29,993 --> 00:27:32,367
Girl, don’t believe him!

537
00:27:32,421 --> 00:27:35,195
You know, guys who look
like that? They’re players!

538
00:27:35,226 --> 00:27:37,494
Wait, wait, wait, who even are you?!

539
00:27:37,592 --> 00:27:40,686
Tash, he’s my cousin!

540
00:27:40,893 --> 00:27:42,399
You don’t believe me?

541
00:27:43,452 --> 00:27:43,999
Huh?

542
00:27:44,024 --> 00:27:45,070
My god! Look at her!

543
00:27:45,095 --> 00:27:48,175
The facial features! The jawline!

544
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:51,836
Look at her cheeks!
Same complexion, right?

545
00:27:52,098 --> 00:27:53,891
Don’t we look alike? She’s my cousin!

546
00:27:53,916 --> 00:27:55,073
Do you believe me now?

547
00:27:55,202 --> 00:27:56,368
Nope!

548
00:27:57,201 --> 00:27:59,860
Then fine. Maybe she’s just my nephew.

549
00:28:00,372 --> 00:28:01,238
Still no!

550
00:28:01,813 --> 00:28:03,673
Karl, do you need anything else?

551
00:28:03,757 --> 00:28:06,263
More food? Juice? What do you want?

552
00:28:06,288 --> 00:28:07,550
Thanks, Cha, I’m good!

553
00:28:07,575 --> 00:28:10,505
- How about water? Water!
- Ah, yeah!

554
00:28:10,583 --> 00:28:12,523
Ah, Lola…thank you, Lola Maxi.

555
00:28:12,628 --> 00:28:13,633
I’m good.

556
00:28:13,658 --> 00:28:16,504
Wow, you guys are really
treating me like royalty!

557
00:28:16,721 --> 00:28:18,382
It’s like this is my last supper!

558
00:28:21,903 --> 00:28:23,363
He said last supper!

559
00:28:23,815 --> 00:28:27,177
Did you hear that, my love?! He said it!

560
00:28:27,202 --> 00:28:30,738
I hope heaven hears us and grants our wish!

561
00:28:34,054 --> 00:28:39,155
Don’t worry, we’ll make
sure he feels loved.

562
00:28:41,355 --> 00:28:42,681
Tso K!

563
00:28:42,785 --> 00:28:43,759
Yes, Mariposa?

564
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:47,140
This is Father Dianelo. Father.

565
00:28:47,165 --> 00:28:49,888
Ah, Father. Good afternoon.

566
00:28:49,913 --> 00:28:51,199
Good afternoon to you.

567
00:28:51,295 --> 00:28:53,669
Wait, why is there a priest?

568
00:28:54,486 --> 00:28:55,840
Simbang Gabi is over, isn’t it?

569
00:28:55,963 --> 00:28:57,643
You’re quite the joker, young man.

570
00:28:58,707 --> 00:29:04,627
Don’t worry, God will forgive
us, and we’ll all enter His kingdom.

571
00:29:05,354 --> 00:29:07,261
I don’t understand.

572
00:29:07,286 --> 00:29:12,535
Ah, well, Tso K, it’s best if you
confess first… before you pass on.

573
00:29:12,885 --> 00:29:16,089
Ah, yeah, con–con–what confession?!

574
00:29:17,030 --> 00:29:19,690
Wait a minute, why
do I need to confess?!

575
00:29:20,139 --> 00:29:21,445
Am I dying?!

576
00:29:21,470 --> 00:29:23,923
Oh, why, Tso K? Aren’t you…?

577
00:29:24,773 --> 00:29:26,280
Aren’t I what?!

578
00:29:26,590 --> 00:29:28,496
I’m perfectly healthy!

579
00:29:30,715 --> 00:29:33,528
Why?! Why would you think that?!

580
00:29:33,825 --> 00:29:34,692
See?!

581
00:29:35,290 --> 00:29:37,436
That’s what I’m saying!

582
00:29:38,398 --> 00:29:43,785
It’s all just rumors!
You’re not even sure!

583
00:29:44,038 --> 00:29:48,241
Well, Kuya Aga, Ash said that his
patients who suddenly become kind…

584
00:29:48,557 --> 00:29:50,390
those are the ones
who are about to die!

585
00:29:50,818 --> 00:29:54,166
Oh, about to die?!

586
00:29:54,321 --> 00:29:56,601
Wait… I’ll deal with that first.

587
00:29:56,646 --> 00:30:02,764
Wait! No!
BFF, no! Relax!

588
00:30:05,312 --> 00:30:08,165
Psst! Where are you going now?!

589
00:30:08,198 --> 00:30:09,351
Just getting some air.

590
00:30:09,376 --> 00:30:11,488
It’s so hot in there, I’ve been sweating.

591
00:30:11,573 --> 00:30:12,379
Good.

592
00:30:12,404 --> 00:30:13,703
Exactly, here I go. Here, here.

593
00:30:15,345 --> 00:30:16,413
BFF?

594
00:30:16,653 --> 00:30:17,744
Karl?

595
00:30:17,769 --> 00:30:18,422
Oh!

596
00:30:18,508 --> 00:30:18,875
Karl!

597
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:21,501
- Tso K!
- BFF! BFF!

598
00:30:30,171 --> 00:30:30,778
Karl!

599
00:30:30,803 --> 00:30:32,178
Fan him, fan ! him, fan him

600
00:30:32,203 --> 00:30:33,395
- Tso K!
- BFF!

601
00:30:34,559 --> 00:30:36,192
It stinks!

602
00:30:36,792 --> 00:30:37,869
It really stinks.

603
00:30:38,345 --> 00:30:39,219
BFF!

604
00:30:39,244 --> 00:30:40,424
- BFF!
- What the heck?!

605
00:30:41,122 --> 00:30:41,715
BFF!

606
00:30:41,783 --> 00:30:42,717
There, there!

607
00:30:45,693 --> 00:30:47,400
I’m in heaven!

608
00:30:47,425 --> 00:30:47,947
Huh?

609
00:30:47,972 --> 00:30:52,320
Tso—Tso K, Tso K, Tso K,
calm down! You’re not in heaven.

610
00:30:52,345 --> 00:30:55,286
- I thought… I’m alive?!
- Yes, you’re alive!

611
00:30:55,870 --> 00:30:59,987
What’s going on with you? You scared us!

612
00:31:00,018 --> 00:31:03,318
- Scared you?!
- Yeah! Karl, what’s really wrong with you?

613
00:31:03,373 --> 00:31:04,279
Wrong with me?!

614
00:31:04,304 --> 00:31:05,377
Yeah, what’s your illness?

615
00:31:05,402 --> 00:31:06,676
I don’t have an illness!

616
00:31:06,898 --> 00:31:09,831
- I just got so annoyed with that woman!
- Huh?!

617
00:31:09,856 --> 00:31:11,906
Why are you spreading false rumors?!

618
00:31:11,931 --> 00:31:13,117
You’re such a gossip!

619
00:31:13,142 --> 00:31:15,918
You know that’s bad, right?
You could ruin someone’s life!

620
00:31:16,463 --> 00:31:19,023
Wait a minute! So, you’re not dying?!

621
00:31:19,361 --> 00:31:20,555
Why? Do you want me to?!

622
00:31:20,580 --> 00:31:22,476
No! It’s not that I want you to die.

623
00:31:22,501 --> 00:31:23,094
Then what?

624
00:31:23,119 --> 00:31:25,693
I was just saying, all that talk about…

625
00:31:26,010 --> 00:31:28,209
I mean, we can’t take all
that with us to heaven, right?

626
00:31:28,249 --> 00:31:34,661
The things we leave behind, the help we
give, the good deeds… You know what I mean!

627
00:31:34,686 --> 00:31:38,305
Ah! Now I get it!

628
00:31:38,330 --> 00:31:40,029
Didn’t you say you were even giving away—

629
00:31:40,054 --> 00:31:42,057
- Like that?!
- Like what?

630
00:31:42,082 --> 00:31:45,243
So, all the good things I was doing,

631
00:31:45,948 --> 00:31:50,741
you guys thought I was doing
them because I was about to die?!

632
00:31:51,154 --> 00:31:52,316
Is that it?!

633
00:31:52,341 --> 00:31:54,901
That’s what you all assumed! Why?

634
00:31:55,139 --> 00:31:56,412
Why do you think like that?!

635
00:31:56,842 --> 00:31:58,995
Can’t a person just change for the better?!

636
00:31:59,199 --> 00:32:02,132
If I want to be kind,
is that not allowed?!

637
00:32:02,157 --> 00:32:03,057
W-w-why?

638
00:32:03,082 --> 00:32:04,983
Why do you guys think like that?!

639
00:32:05,008 --> 00:32:06,303
Judging right away?!

640
00:32:07,735 --> 00:32:10,268
No, no, no. Nobody was thinking that.

641
00:32:10,523 --> 00:32:13,136
Now, I understand everything.

642
00:32:13,802 --> 00:32:17,114
So, because of the
good things I did for you,

643
00:32:17,139 --> 00:32:20,739
you really thought I
was dying, and you were

644
00:32:20,763 --> 00:32:24,503
just being nice to make
me feel better?!

645
00:32:25,492 --> 00:32:26,559
That’s so messed up!

646
00:32:27,433 --> 00:32:30,433
BFF, if we didn’t love you,

647
00:32:30,906 --> 00:32:32,739
we wouldn’t care
about you at all.

648
00:32:33,628 --> 00:32:39,568
And all the kindness we showed
you, Karl, that came from our hearts!

649
00:32:39,593 --> 00:32:40,521
Of course!

650
00:32:40,546 --> 00:32:41,921
That’s right.

651
00:32:42,132 --> 00:32:45,659
We even prayed for you
because we were worried.

652
00:32:45,684 --> 00:32:47,599
We don’t want to lose you.

653
00:32:47,774 --> 00:32:49,394
We wanted a miracle.

654
00:32:49,419 --> 00:32:50,534
Really?

655
00:32:50,559 --> 00:32:51,680
Yes!

656
00:32:52,080 --> 00:32:52,780
Is that true?

657
00:32:52,864 --> 00:32:54,037
Yes.

658
00:32:56,920 --> 00:32:58,720
S-sorry.

659
00:32:59,050 --> 00:33:03,197
I just assumed based on my
experience with my elderly patients.

660
00:33:03,228 --> 00:33:04,890
Elderly—elderly?!

661
00:33:05,149 --> 00:33:06,502
I’m forty-eight!

662
00:33:06,527 --> 00:33:07,695
You’re forty-eight?

663
00:33:08,414 --> 00:33:12,311
No… well… yeah, you got me. It’s like…

664
00:33:17,755 --> 00:33:23,546
BFF, I just want to
apologize if we hurt you.

665
00:33:24,727 --> 00:33:27,601
We don’t want you to… die.

666
00:33:28,140 --> 00:33:29,460
Who would want that, right?

667
00:33:29,485 --> 00:33:31,526
Y-you? You want to get hurt?

668
00:33:31,612 --> 00:33:32,152
Why?

669
00:33:32,177 --> 00:33:33,392
You’re still… you’re still…

670
00:33:33,417 --> 00:33:34,263
Still what?

671
00:33:34,288 --> 00:33:35,294
You still have your arm around her!

672
00:33:35,319 --> 00:33:36,371
My arm around you?

673
00:33:36,742 --> 00:33:37,535
Oh, right!

674
00:33:37,560 --> 00:33:38,866
I didn’t even notice that! Huh?

675
00:33:38,979 --> 00:33:40,406
Where am I?

676
00:33:40,850 --> 00:33:42,436
What’s happening to me here?

677
00:33:43,047 --> 00:33:45,014
Why am I hugging? Am I hugging?!

678
00:33:47,094 --> 00:33:48,241
I didn’t even realize!

679
00:33:48,266 --> 00:33:49,769
- Tso K, Tso K, Tso K!
- Tso K, Tso K, Tso K!

680
00:33:49,794 --> 00:33:51,098
Let’s measure it, okay? There!

681
00:33:51,123 --> 00:33:54,070
What do you want—narra,
kamagong, or bamboo?

682
00:33:54,095 --> 00:33:55,114
Bamboo is really sturdy!

683
00:33:55,139 --> 00:33:57,681
We have a buy-one-take-one
deal today! If you don’t

684
00:33:57,705 --> 00:34:00,195
like one coffin, you can
switch to another one.

685
00:34:00,220 --> 00:34:03,257
And if you’re not into
coffins… we also have urns!

686
00:34:03,282 --> 00:34:05,262
Twenty percent off! Oh,
wait—twenty-five percent!

687
00:34:05,333 --> 00:34:05,713
Hey!

688
00:34:05,738 --> 00:34:06,706
What color do you want?

689
00:34:07,185 --> 00:34:08,372
- Color?
- Yeah.

690
00:34:08,411 --> 00:34:10,170
- For the coffin and the urn?
- Yes.

691
00:34:10,195 --> 00:34:11,581
We’re already measuring, Father!

692
00:34:11,974 --> 00:34:13,374
Wait, wait, wait!

693
00:34:13,763 --> 00:34:16,670
Why are you all so
busy planning this?!

694
00:34:16,930 --> 00:34:18,757
It’s like you actually want me to go first!

695
00:34:18,958 --> 00:34:21,798
Don’t worry, I’m not going anywhere.

696
00:34:21,869 --> 00:34:22,875
Then… who’s going first?

697
00:34:22,900 --> 00:34:24,540
You’re going first!

698
00:34:25,685 --> 00:34:27,378
No, no, no, no!

699
00:34:39,850 --> 00:34:40,929
Orb…

700
00:34:41,075 --> 00:34:42,118
What?

701
00:34:42,143 --> 00:34:43,093
Are you Google?

702
00:34:44,871 --> 00:34:46,187
Why?

703
00:34:46,667 --> 00:34:49,874
Because everything I’ve
been looking for is in you.

704
00:34:57,572 --> 00:35:00,007
Anne, sorry for what happened.

705
00:35:00,941 --> 00:35:02,687
Communication really is the key.

706
00:35:03,668 --> 00:35:06,304
That will be my first resolution.

707
00:35:08,633 --> 00:35:11,719
Our first LQ? I hope it’s the last.

708
00:35:28,662 --> 00:35:30,675
Work from Singapore called.

709
00:35:53,079 --> 00:35:55,712
We’ll tell Mom and Dad we’re
going back to Singapore, okay?

710
00:35:55,745 --> 00:35:58,005
What?! You’re leaving?!

711
00:35:58,030 --> 00:35:59,451
- Ssssh!
- Wait!

712
00:35:59,523 --> 00:36:02,315
I can’t keep secrets.

713
00:36:02,434 --> 00:36:04,761
Especially about Anne and Andres.

714
00:36:04,786 --> 00:36:08,296
- What?! You and Anne are together?!
- Sssh! Don’t say it out loud!

715
00:36:08,321 --> 00:36:11,359
Tso K, what if I get a boyfriend?

716
00:36:11,450 --> 00:36:12,683
A boyfriend?!

717
00:36:13,049 --> 00:36:14,316
Where is he?!

718
00:36:14,397 --> 00:36:15,897
Bring him here so I
can break his legs!

719
00:36:15,922 --> 00:36:18,388
Uh… Tso K, I’m heading home.
Okay, bye-bye! Thank you!

720
00:36:18,487 --> 00:36:20,621
- I have something to tell you.
- Huh?

721
00:36:20,646 --> 00:36:22,320
I have a serious illness.

722
00:36:22,526 --> 00:36:26,099
What?! You’re dying?!

723
00:36:26,273 --> 00:36:28,913
Get a massage here, it’s really good.

724
00:36:28,982 --> 00:36:30,929
- Alright, Kuya Aga! Enjoy!
- Okay!

725
00:36:31,754 --> 00:36:34,367
It’s late, my husband is probably waiting.

726
00:36:35,707 --> 00:36:37,267
- Why?
- He’s inside.

727
00:36:37,600 --> 00:36:38,227
Huh?!
